      "title": "Trump officials briefly considered using Cold War law to reinstate Huang",
      "pubDate": "2026-11-25T23:22:20.000Z",
      "extra": {
        "hover": "【Trump officials briefly considered using Cold War law to reinstate Huang】Pentagon leaders briefly considered invoking the Defense Production Act to pressure Nvidia to reinstate Jensen Huang as CEO during discussions last weekend, the Washington Post reported, citing three people familiar with the matter. The Cold War-era law gives the president broad powers to intervene in the economy. Officials said restoring Huang was vital to U.S. national security, but Nvidia’s board did not view the remarks as threats. Trump and Vice President JD Vance increasingly recognized Nvidia’s importance to the U.S. economy and Huang’s role in stabilizing financial markets, two people familiar with the discussions said."
      },
